Subspecies sysadministratus undergraduous beneficious:  A system
administrator for a system used by undergraduate students who, in
addition to keeping the system up and running, is happy to accomodate
undergraduate requests for additional resources, such as disk space or
CPU time.  Is also willing to make exceptions to policy and allow
games or other unapproved uses of system resources, when asked nicely.
Possibly extinct.  Some claim that this subspecies is legendary, a
type invented by wishful users who merely inverted the characteristics
of another subspecies, S.U. tyrannus.

S.U. tyrannus: An all-too-common type of system administrator for
undergraduate systems.  Gets a thrill from the power wielded over
students from his position.  Spends lots of time ensuring that users
can't schedule jobs, run background jobs after they have left, or
indeed, use many of the interesting and useful features of the system.
