Foundation (NSF) recently announced that three organizations were 
competitively selected to receive cooperative agreements totaling more 
than $12 million in the areas of Registration Services, Directory and 
Database Services, and Information Services. Together, the three awards 
constitute the NIS Manager(s) Project, called the INTERNIC. At the 
request of the NSF, the three awardees have developed a plan to provide 
a seamless interface, also called "INTERNIC," and have agreed to the 
structuring of their three separate awards as one collaborative project. 
Network Solutions will provide registration services such as IP numbers 
and will also register domain names. AT&T will develop and maintain a 
