I'd like to disagree with Monica and others on the need to ask permission
of subjects AFTER the semester for the right to use material related to
their participation in a discussion.  The role of the Institutional
Research Board is to protect the rights and privacy of individual human
subjects.  The researcher should have the research design reviewed and
approved (including the manner in which data is collected, used, distributed,
and destroyed, as well as the indentities of participants protected).  Once
the research is carried out and completed, to then ask subjects for
permission to use the collected data eviscerates the study.  The research
review process was instituted to insure that individuals were protected, but
enabling research to go forward.

