We should also include "privacy" alongside "integrity and completeness."
This document requires service providers to provide privacy; however, 
the service itself may offer ample opportunity for the user to render
their own data public.  (Unix chmod, ACLs, etc.)  If an admin sees that
a user has made some data public, are we to assume that they *intended*
to do so?

