     Vex Populi: NBC News commentator John Chancellor displayed
his contempt for mainstream America again during a recent chat at
Columbia University.  Chancellor dismissed the influence of radio
talk show hosts on the political process, saying that he
sometimes worries that "talk show America is going to dominate
the dialogue, and that we are all going to be pushed into
positions that we may find harmful to the country by too much vox
populi."
      Chancellor realized his comments sounded undemocratic
elitist.  However, he attempted to justify them, saying that "the
problems that face America today are very complicated problems,"
and he didn't think that you could "solve them by getting a lot
of people down in the agora and letting them all shout or vote or
drop pebbles in pails." Chancellor summed up his thoughts, saying
" I think you need a better way to run this country and elect
people than just turning it all over to the people."

